@startuml
title How the six equations actually execute: the unconditional nu-float to a normal form

skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #374151
skinparam activity {
  BorderColor #1F2937
  FontColor #111827
}

start

:**a term arrives at the seam**
""Language::try_direct_eval"" or
""dovetail_report_for""; <<#DBEAFE>>
note right #DBEAFE
  Gate (""should_emit_binder_congruence"",
  macros/src/gen/runtime/binder_congruence.rs:59):
  the handler is emitted iff the language
  (1) declares equations,
  (2) has NO ""RhoNativeJoin"" host obligation,
  (3) has a surface SINGLE-binder constructor.
  Ambient satisfies all three; Rholang fails (2).
end note

repeat
  :**one bottom-up float pass** (""__bcn_float_pass""); <<#F3F4F6>>

  partition "prefix and ambient arms - InNew, OutNew, OpenNew, AmbNew" {
    :normalise the body;
    if (is the normalised body a ""PNew""?) then (yes)
      :""scope.unbind()"" - **freshen** the binder to a
      process-global gensym, then open the scope; <<#FEF3C7>>
      note right #FEF3C7
        The freshness premise <latex>x \# N</latex> is NOT checked.
        It is discharged **by construction**: a globally
        fresh binder cannot occur free in any pre-existing
        sibling or field, so re-closing captures nothing.
        The generated ""is_fresh"" in freshness.rs survives
        as a live public API with no caller.
      end note
      :rebuild the prefix INSIDE the scope; <<#FEF3C7>>
      :""Scope::new"" - re-close, recomputing the
      de Bruijn coordinates locally; <<#FEF3C7>>
    else (no)
      :leave the node as it is;
    endif
  }

  partition "bag arm - ScopeExtrusion" {
    if (does some bag member normalise to a ""PNew""?) then (yes)
      :remove that member; the remaining
      multiset is the residual; <<#DCFCE7>>
      :""unbind"" the member's scope; <<#DCFCE7>>
      :**splice** the opened body into the widened
      bag via ""insert_into_ppar""; <<#FEE2E2>>
      note right #FEE2E2
        **AM-2, the flatness obligation.** If the opened body
        is itself a ""PPar"", pushing it as ONE element yields
        <latex>\{\{A,B\},C\}</latex>. Cardelli-Gordon dissolves that by
        (Struct Par Assoc) - a law this fragment absorbs only
        REPRESENTATIONALLY, so nothing would ever flatten it
        and sibling redexes would stay hidden. The splice is
        what keeps the bag flat.
      end note
      :re-close the widened bag under
      the freshened binder; <<#DCFCE7>>
    else (no)
      :rebuild the bag from
      the normalised members;
    endif
  }

  partition "restriction arm - NewComm" {
    :collect the maximal run of adjacent ""PNew"" binders; <<#EDE9FE>>
    :re-close the run in the permutation that MINIMISES
    the alpha-canonical semantic key (runs longer
    than 6 binders are left in declaration order); <<#EDE9FE>>
    note right #EDE9FE
      (Struct Res Res) realised as a CANONICAL ORDER
      rather than as a rewrite: two terms differing only
      by the order of a nu-run reach the SAME normal
      form, so the equation holds by construction.
    end note
  }

repeat while (did this pass change the term? (""BoundTerm::term_eq"")) is (yes, fuel remains)
-> no - fixpoint reached;

:**restriction-normal form**: every ""new"" has floated
as far outward as it can go, and the soup
underneath is FLAT; <<#DBEAFE>>

if (did anything change at all?) then (yes)
  :""Some(nf)"" - the floated term is what enters the
  Dovetail e-graph, where the three capability
  rules match the soup; <<#DCFCE7>>
  :**redexes that were split across a restriction
  are now syntactically adjacent, and fire**; <<#DCFCE7>>
else (no)
  :""None"" - the fail-closed seam is preserved:
  no progress is claimed; <<#FEE2E2>>
endif

stop

@enduml
